---
import Term from "../Term.astro";
import "./sternzeit.css";
---

<figure class="moon-figure">
    <div class="moon-view" data-export="moon">
        <button type="button" class="view-toggle" data-field="lockMoon" aria-pressed="false" title="Lock the view to the Moon itself: north up, no horizon">moon-locked</button>
        <svg viewBox="-100 -100 200 200" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
        <p class="moon-status" data-field="status"></p>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The Moon as seen from the chosen place, zenith up: lit by the Sun (arrow), its night side in{" "}
        <Term of="Earthshine">earthshine</Term> (blue rays, longer when stronger). The grid is the Moon's own, its
        center shifted by the <Term of="Libration">libration</Term> (arrow, from its mean center to the point we
        look at) and its north pole (N) turned, against the zenith (dashed), by the{" "}
        <Term of="Position angle of axis">position angle of the axis</Term> and the{" "}
        <Term of="Parallactic angle">parallactic angle</Term> (arc). The dashed circles are its size at apogee and perigee.
        Magnified, with the horizon at the same scale. The button in the corner locks the view to the Moon itself,
        its north up and the horizon gone, leaving the librations as the only motion.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./moonview.js";
</script>
